# .privacy-email-allowlist — known-safe email addresses/domains that are NOT third-party PII.
# Used by scripts/audit-privacy.sh (P936). An email in an ADDED diff line that matches NO
# entry here is flagged as a possible third-party PII leak.
#
# Scope: the email check runs on added diff lines AND commit messages (since the P1438 follow-up;
# Co-Authored-By trailers are noreply@ addresses, covered below). Existing emails in untouched files are
# not re-scanned (the scanner only sees added/modified lines), so this list need only cover
# addresses/domains that legitimately recur in NEW commits — not every address in the tree.
#
# Grammar (one entry per line; case-insensitive; '#' = comment; blank lines ignored):
#   example.com          bare domain          -> any address @example.com
#   *.example.com        domain-suffix        -> any address whose domain ends .example.com
#   noreply@*            local-part wildcard   -> any address with local part 'noreply'
#   jack@greensock.com   full address          -> that exact address only
#   tel:15550100         phone, exact          -> that number (digits only; + and spaces ignored)
#   tel:1555*            phone, digit prefix   -> any number starting with those digits
#
# To add a safe address: append the NARROWEST entry that covers it. Prefer @example.com for
# NEW test fixtures over allowlisting a real domain. A real third-party person's address does
# NOT belong here — anonymize it instead (.claude/rules/features.md, "PII in Specs").

# --- RFC-reserved / placeholder test domains ---
example.com
*.example.com
example-test.com
example.invalid
example.co.uk
*.example.co.uk
test.com
test.example
email.com
yourdomain.com
domain.tld
bar.com
company.com
mail.company.com

# --- fictional phone ranges reserved for fiction/tests (use these in fixtures) ---
# +1 555 ... (NANP area code 555 is not assigned to any region) and Ofcom 07700 900xxx (UK drama
# range). NOTE: the classic NANP fiction range is <any area code>-555-01xx, which a digit-prefix
# entry cannot express — for fixtures use +1 555 ... or +44 7700 900 ... instead.
tel:1555*
tel:447700900*

# --- project domains ---
claritypledge.com
*.claritypledge.com

# --- known-safe service / infra hostnames (config/docs artifacts, not personal PII) ---
*.ingest.sentry.io
*.supabase.com
*.supabase.co
*.gserviceaccount.com
group.calendar.google.com
users.noreply.github.com
noreply@*

